The progression makes observing frame, epoch, angle and unit explicit; derives parallax geometry and separates positive physical distance from potentially negative measured parallax; models photon counts, background variance and shared calibration; distinguishes flux from luminosity and spectral density conventions; and exposes distance/extinction, transit/dilution and orbital/inclination ambiguities. Thermal spectra and cosmological geometry are declared model inputs, not falsely derived from the earlier finite quantum exercises.

The connected systems account derives circular binary projection and mass relations, introduces stellar mass/pressure/energy balances, distinguishes stellar populations from a single evolutionary movie, and bounds spherical circular mass inference. The uniform-density star is an original limited model; changing density at fixed C changes its physical G relation. The flat expansion example prescribes a(t)=(t/t0)^2 and derives redshift, light-travel and distance relations. It is neither a fitted universe nor a claimed solution of Einstein equations. Nuclear rates, full stellar transport/evolution, cosmological dynamics and specialist observing remain later formation.

Selected OpenStax *Astronomy 2e* passages were inspected for parallax, brightness, thermal radiation, stellar balance/classification, galactic rotation, expansion and thermal/background-radiation evidence. Larger assigned chapters are distinguished from actual inspected passages. The accepted Bailer-Jones and colleagues Gaia EDR3 distance manuscript opening and author FAQ ground inverse-parallax, prior, selection and zero-point limits; no catalogue or raw-observation analysis is claimed. The Hubble 1929 source was a university-hosted five-page transcription of the six-page PNAS article, not an original facsimile. Its actual tables and surrounding qualifications were inspected. Source/component rights remain stated separately; source media stay external.

The bounded Hubble table reconstruction uses NGC 278: v=650 km/s, solar term −110 km/s and assumed K=500 km/s/Mpc give r=1.52 Mpc. Apparent magnitude 12 gives absolute magnitude −13.9092179397…, rounding to the table's −13.9. The distance was inferred using K, so it cannot independently validate K. Historical parameters are not presented as current cosmological estimates. Original fixtures also show that rescaling all distances changes a fitted slope without changing its predictions/residuals.

