The eighth physics block is installed after `@physics-rotation-review`. Its ten new lessons are `physics-statistical-states`, `physics-statistical-constraints`, `physics-statistical-entropy`, `physics-statistical-reservoir`, `physics-statistical-canonical`, `physics-statistical-fluctuations`, `physics-statistical-countable`, `physics-statistical-dynamics`, `physics-statistical-study`, `physics-statistical-review`. Physics now has **98 common learning Records**. No new source identity was created; the existing `@mat-tong-statistical` source, mathematical counting/series/truncation, inquiry probability and thermodynamic/chemical-potential formation are reused by reference. Their learning routes remain unchanged.

The block begins with labeled localized two-state sites, making the spectrum, energy additivity, accessible set and equal-weight premise explicit. Its isolated fixture has eight sites and three excitations, with three observed sites. The observed count distribution is (10,30,15,1)/56, mean 9/8 and variance 225/448. An independent canonical model with excitation ratio 3/5 instead has distribution (125,225,135,27)/512, the same mean and variance 45/64. The covariance derivation shows why fixed total energy prevents subsystem independence even when energies add. The fixed-subsystem reservoir limit is proved without claiming global equality of ensembles.

Entropy formation distinguishes a whole distribution, a particular macrostate and the grouped entropy decomposition. The block connects energy-sharing maxima to entropy slopes and stability conditions, retains the earlier thermodynamic second-law premises, and does not derive a relaxation law from counting. Finite reservoir weights precede the canonical approximation; a finite Taylor remainder controls probability ratios only on a common valid support. Canonical differentiation, fixed-level heat capacity, entropy/Helmholtz identities and the finite relative-entropy minimum are derived with their conditions. Correlation counterexamples and concentration bounds distinguish model fluctuation from measurement uncertainty and sample inference.

The countable two-mode energy ladder reuses the preceding mathematics proofs and `series_study.py` unchanged. Its physical spectrum remains stipulated, not derived quantum mechanics. Energy units and observable-specific tail error are restored, and finite-spectrum versus infinite-spectrum endpoint behavior is explicit. The kinetics lesson separately specifies a binary Markov model: transition pairs (1/6,1/3) and (1/12,1/6) have the same stationary excitation 1/3 but different relaxation. From an excited initial state their third-step probabilities are 5/12 and 59/96. Three stationary samples under the first pair have mean-variance 11/81 rather than the independent 2/27. Periodic/identity boundaries and a stationary directed cycle expose invalid claims about equilibration and detailed balance.

The original investigation requires a connected report, a discriminating evidence plan, a changed-spectrum/interaction extension, independent derivation, criticism and revision. Exact finite checks establish authored calculations and programs; no real material, apparatus, observed learner performance, empirical relaxation rate or experiment is claimed. Source assignments remain broader than passage inspection.

